{"name":"Storm Warning","hex":"#696863","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"storm","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any disturbed state of the atmosphere causing destructive or unpleasant weather, especially one affecting the earth's surface involving strong winds (leading to high waves at sea) and usually lightning, thunder, and precipitation.","A heavy fall of precipitation (hail, rain, or snow) or bout of lightning and thunder without strong winds; a hail storm, rainstorm, snowstorm, or thunderstorm."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["Preceded by the dummy subject it: to have strong winds and usually lightning and thunder, and/or hail, rain, or snow.","To make (someone or something) stormy; to agitate (someone or something) violently.\n\n\nTo disturb or trouble (someone)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/storm"},{"term":"warning","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["present participle of warn"]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An instance of warning someone.","Something spoken or written that is intended to warn."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/warning"}],"entries":[{"title":"Storm warning","blocks":[{"text":"At sea, a storm warning is a warning issued by the National Weather Service of the United States when winds between 48 and 63 knots are occurring or predicted to occur soon. The winds must not be associated with a tropical cyclone. If the winds are associated with a tropical cyclone, a tropical storm warning will be substituted for the storm warning and less severe gale warning."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/db/Weather_Warning_Flag_%28United_States%29.svg/330px-Weather_Warning_Flag_%28United_States%29.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Storm_warning","wikidata":"Q2874402"},{"title":"Storm Warning (Higgins novel)","blocks":[{"text":"Storm Warning is a 1976 novel by Jack Higgins The novel was Higgins's next after his 1975 bestseller The Eagle Has Landed."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/a/a5/StormWarning.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Storm_Warning_(Higgins_novel)","wikidata":"Q7620186"},{"title":"Storm Warning (1950 film)","blocks":[{"text":"Storm Warning is a 1950 American thriller film noir starring Ginger Rogers, Ronald Reagan, Doris Day, and Steve Cochran. Directed by Stuart Heisler, it follows a fashion model (Rogers), traveling to a small Southern town to visit her sister (Day), who witnesses the brutal murder of an investigative journalist by the Ku Klux Klan (KKK). The original screenplay was written by Richard Brooks and Daniel Fuchs."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/2/28/Stormwarningposter.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Storm_Warning_(1950_film)","wikidata":"Q2385766"},{"title":"Storm","blocks":[{"text":"A storm is any disturbed state of the natural environment or the atmosphere of an astronomical body. It may be marked by significant disruptions to normal conditions such as strong wind, tornadoes, hail, thunder and lightning, heavy precipitation, heavy freezing rain, strong winds, wind transporting some substance through the atmosphere such as in a dust storm, among other forms of severe weather."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/Cloud_cumulonimbus_at_baltic_sea%281%29.jpg/330px-Cloud_cumulonimbus_at_baltic_sea%281%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Storm","wikidata":"Q81054"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1b/Storm_Warning_-_Ginger_Rogers_finale_trailer_screenshot.jpg/500px-Storm_Warning_-_Ginger_Rogers_finale_trailer_screenshot.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1b/Storm_Warning_-_Ginger_Rogers_finale_trailer_screenshot.jpg/500px-Storm_Warning_-_Ginger_Rogers_finale_trailer_screenshot.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Marsha (center), played by Ginger Rogers, in the film's climactic finale","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AStorm_Warning_-_Ginger_Rogers_finale_trailer_screenshot.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1b/Ginger_Rogers_by_John_Miehle_6.jpg/500px-Ginger_Rogers_by_John_Miehle_6.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1b/Ginger_Rogers_by_John_Miehle_6.jpg/500px-Ginger_Rogers_by_John_Miehle_6.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGinger_Rogers_by_John_Miehle_6.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/Lauren_Bacall_-_YankArmyWeekly_detail.jpg/250px-Lauren_Bacall_-_YankArmyWeekly_detail.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/1/1d/Lauren_Bacall_-_YankArmyWeekly_detail.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1d/Lauren_Bacall_-_YankArmyWeekly_detail.jpg/250px-Lauren_Bacall_-_YankArmyWeekly_detail.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ALauren_Bacall_-_YankArmyWeekly_detail.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b3/Storm_Warning_trailer_tagline_%28They_hide_a_thousand_vicious_crimes%29.jpg/500px-Storm_Warning_trailer_tagline_%28They_hide_a_thousand_vicious_crimes%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wi